**APPROVE FOR TESTING**

No blockers found. Below is the verification of each review point against the updated inline code and protocol doc.

### 1. `PanicSafeFuture` & `async-task` 4.7.1 `drop_future` Abort Protection
- **Separate Unwind Boundaries**: [`PanicSafeFuture::poll`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-runnable/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L94-L112) wraps the inner future poll in `catch_unwind`. On `Ok(Poll::Ready(()))` or `Err(_)` (poll panic), it transitions out of the poll unwind before invoking [`PanicSafeFuture::dispose`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-runnable/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L86-L90), which takes `self.0` and drops the boxed inner future inside a second, independent `catch_unwind`.
- **No Abort in `async-task` `raw.rs`**: Because `PanicSafeFuture::poll` catches any poll panic, disposes `self.0` (setting it to `None`), and returns `Poll::Ready(())`, `async-task` sees a normal completion. When `async-task` subsequently drops the outer `PanicSafeFuture` inside `drop_future` (or if `PanicSafeFuture::drop` runs during cancellation/teardown), `self.0` is already `None` (or caught by `dispose()` in [`Drop::drop`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-runnable/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L114-L118)), so `PanicSafeFuture`'s destructor never unwinds into `async-task`'s `abort_on_panic` guard.
- **Lease Safety**: The [`Lease`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-runnable/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L73-L80) is moved into the boxed inner `async move` future in [`Pool::spawn`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-runnable/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L482-L486). Even if the user future panics during `poll` and/or its destructor panics during `dispose()`, the `Lease` field in the outer generated future state machine is still dropped during `drop(self.0.take())`, decrementing `active.count` and notifying `idle`.

### 2. No Per-Poll `Mutex` or `Arc<Job>` Clone on `Runnable` Path
- `PanicSafeFuture` holds `Option<FutureJob>` (`Pin<Box<dyn Future<Output = ()> + Send + 'static>>`) directly without a `Mutex`, relying on `async-task::Runnable`'s state machine for exclusive poll access.
- `Work::Runnable(async_task::Runnable<TaskMeta>)` moves the unique `Runnable` ticket through the split queue and `schedule` closure without cloning an `Arc<Job>` per poll.

### 3. Retained Wakers & Completed Job Resurrection
- `task.detach()` is called before `runnable.schedule()` in [`Pool::spawn`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-runnable/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L510-L511).
- Once `PanicSafeFuture::poll` returns `Poll::Ready(())`, `async-task` marks the task completed and drops the future before releasing the state machine; any cloned `Waker` invoked after completion is a no-op in `async-task` and will never re-invoke the schedule closure or re-poll `PanicSafeFuture` (covered by [`completed_job_ignores_retained_waker`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-runnable/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L761-L780)).
- If a waker fires *during* `poll` just before `PanicSafeFuture` returns `Poll::Ready(())` (e.g., on panic or ready), `async-task`'s state transition on `Poll::Ready` consumes the notified bit and completes the task rather than re-scheduling it.

### 4. Regression Test & Documentation Accuracy
- [`native_jobs_survive_future_destructor_panics`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-runnable/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L669-L709) tests both `Policy::Root` and `Policy::Runnable` across `panic_in_poll = false` (completion + destructor panic) and `panic_in_poll = true` (poll panic + destructor panic across separate unwind boundaries), then verifies a subsequent job runs (`42`) and `pool.shutdown()` succeeds cleanly (proving `Lease` was released in both failure modes).
- Both the comments in [`dispatcher.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-runnable/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L81-L85) and [`RUNNABLE-DRIVER-PROTOCOL.md`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-runnable/benchmarks/RUNNABLE-DRIVER-PROTOCOL.md#L18-L26) accurately document that the inner future remains boxed (`FutureJob`) and explicitly state not to claim a single-allocation layout.
